# Mermaid Section

## Purpose

Defines the Mermaid section of the MAM specification. The section uses the Mermaid diagramming language to create visual representations that help humans understand systems, processes, and relationships.

## Inputs

| Name | Type | Required | Description |
|------|------|----------|-------------|
| content | string | Yes | Full MAM module text that contains the section |
| diagram | string | No | Mermaid diagram source to validate directly |

## Outputs

| Name | Type | Description |
|------|------|-------------|
| diagrams | list | Extracted Mermaid diagrams |
| valid | bool | Whether the diagrams pass validation |
| errors | list | Validation errors found in the diagrams |

## Capabilities

### validate

Checks diagram type, completeness, labels, and secrets.

### extract

Pulls the Mermaid diagrams out of the section body.

### document

Renders the diagrams into a documentation fragment.

## Rules

- Code must be valid Mermaid.
- Diagrams should be complete and understandable.
- All nodes should have clear labels.
- Use consistent styling throughout.
- Never include secrets or sensitive data.
- Document any assumptions in the diagrams.
- Group related elements with subgraphs.

## Workflow

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A[Content] --> B[Extract]
    B --> C[Validate]
    C --> D[Document]
    D --> E[Output]
```

## Python

```python
def extract_mermaid(content: str) -> list:
    diagrams = []
    in_mermaid = False
    current = []
    for line in content.split("\n"):
        if line.strip().startswith("```mermaid"):
            in_mermaid = True
            current = []
        elif line.strip() == "```" and in_mermaid:
            in_mermaid = False
            diagrams.append("\n".join(current))
        elif in_mermaid:
            current.append(line)
    return diagrams

def validate_mermaid_diagram(code: str) -> dict:
    errors = []
    valid_types = ["flowchart", "sequenceDiagram", "classDiagram",
                   "stateDiagram", "erDiagram", "gantt", "pie",
                   "mindmap", "timeline"]
    lines = code.strip().split("\n")
    first_line = lines[0] if lines else ""
    if not any(t in first_line for t in valid_types):
        errors.append("Invalid diagram type")
    if len(lines) < 3:
        errors.append("Diagram too short")
    if "password" in code.lower() or "secret" in code.lower():
        errors.append("Diagram contains sensitive data")
    return {"valid": len(errors) == 0, "errors": errors}

def check_labels(code: str) -> bool:
    lines = code.strip().split("\n")
    return all("[" in line or "(" in line or "[" in line for line in lines[1:])

def document_diagram(code: str) -> str:
    first_line = code.strip().split("\n")[0]
    diagram_type = first_line.split()[0]
    return "## " + diagram_type.title() + " Diagram\n\n```mermaid\n" + code + "\n```"
```

## Tests

### Input

```yaml
content: |
  ## Mermaid

  flowchart TD
      A[Start] --> B[Process]
      B --> C[End]
```

### Expected

```yaml
valid: true
errors: []
```

```python
def test_mermaid():
    code = "flowchart TD\n    A[Start] --> B[Process]\n    B --> C[End]"
    assert validate_mermaid_diagram(code)["valid"] is True
    assert check_labels(code)
    assert "Flowchart Diagram" in document_diagram(code)
    assert len(extract_mermaid("```mermaid\n" + code + "\n```")) == 1
```

## Examples

### Architecture Diagram

```mermaid
flowchart TB
    subgraph Frontend
        A[Web App] --> B[API Client]
    end
    subgraph Backend
        C[API Gateway] --> D[Auth Service]
    end
    B --> C
```

### Sequence Diagram

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant U as User
    participant C as Client
    participant A as API
    U->>C: Login Request
    C->>A: POST /auth/login
    A-->>C: Token
    C-->>U: Login Success
```

